  "status": "published",
  "title": "Rain Barrel Collection System",
  "summary": "A 55 gal food-grade drum fed by a downspout diverter, with a brass spigot near the bottom and an overflow line up top. Waters the garden for free.",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "estimatedHours": 3,
  "imageUrl": null,
  "currency": "USD",
  "steps": [
    "Rinse the drum out with water and a little dish soap, and set it on two courses of concrete blocks beside the downspout so a watering can fits under the spigot.",
    "Drill a hole for the spigot bulkhead 3 in above the drum's bottom with the step bit, sized to the fitting's instructions.",
    "Wrap the spigot threads with three turns of PTFE tape, fit the bulkhead with its gaskets inside and out, and tighten it hand-tight plus a quarter turn.",
    "Fit a second bulkhead 3 in below the top for the overflow and screw a short garden hose to it, routed away from the house foundation.",
    "Cut into the downspout at the height of the drum top, install the diverter per its instructions, and run its hose into the inlet hole in the lid.",
    "Cover the lid opening with mosquito mesh held down by a bungee cord, then run water down the downspout and check every fitting for drips."
  ],
